{number: 66}
{title: Out of My Bondage, Sorrow, and Night}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Out of my bondage, sorrow and night,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come, Jesus, I [Ab] come;
Into Thy freedom, gladness and light,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
Out of my [Db] sickness into Thy [Ab] health,
Out of my [Db] want and into Thy [Ab] wealth,
Out of my [Db] sin and into Thy-[Ab] self,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] Out of my shameful failure and loss,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come, Jesus, I [Ab] come;
Into the glorious gain of Thy cross,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
Out of earth's [Db] sorrows into Thy [Ab] balm,
Out of life's [Db] storms and into Thy [Ab] calm,
Out of dis-[Db] tress to jubilant [Ab] psalm,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Out of unrest and arrogant pride,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come, Jesus, I [Ab] come;
Into Thy blessed will to abide,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
Out of my-[Db] self to dwell in Thy [Ab] love,
Out of de-[Db] spair into raptures a-[Ab] bove,
Upward for [Db] aye on wings like a [Ab] dove,
Jesus, I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
